@startuml 07-interfaces
' =====================================================================
' Key interfaces and extension points
' Traces to: FR-23, FR-24, FR-37..FR-40, NFR-3, NFR-4, NFR-11
'
' Shaped by AD-2: we ship a library, not a runner. The instructor's
' test suite calls us, and her run_autograder invokes our AI phase.
' There is therefore no ITestRunner and no IMarkingHook -- running
' tests and deciding what needs feedback are both ordinary code in her
' suite.
' =====================================================================

title Key Interfaces and Extension Points

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0

' ---------------------------------------------------------------------
' What the instructor writes. Not ours.
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------
package "Written by the instructor" #FFF2CC {
  class "Instructor Test Suite" as ITS #FFF2CC {
    Ordinary JUnit or pytest. Calls
    the reporting library with the
    target names registered in the
    web app.
    --
    Under the AUTOGRADER policy, the
    marking logic lives here: any
    condition she can express in code
    can decide whether a target gets
    AI feedback.
  }
}

' ---------------------------------------------------------------------
' The library the instructor's suite calls -- Student C
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------
package "Reporting Library (Student C)" #FBE6D4 {

  interface IReportingClient <<abstract>> {
    +record_outcome(target, test_name,\n status, output, earned_score) : None
    +request_ai_feedback(target, note) : None
    --
    The entire surface the instructor
    touches. Two calls. Keep it this
    small.
  }

  class JavaReporter {
    Shipped as a jar for JUnit suites.
  }

  class PythonReporter {
    Shipped as a package for pytest.
  }

  class FakeReporter {
    Records calls in memory. Lets the
    instructor guide's examples and
    our own tests run offline.
  }

  IReportingClient <|.. JavaReporter
  IReportingClient <|.. PythonReporter
  IReportingClient <|.. FakeReporter

  note as N_TGT #FFF8DC
    **Validate the target name on the first
    call.** These identifiers cross a process
    boundary as bare strings, typed once in the
    web app and again in the suite. A mismatch
    must fail the instructor's test run loudly,
    not record an outcome against nothing.
    See OQ-12.
  end note
}

ITS ..> IReportingClient

' ---------------------------------------------------------------------
' AI phase entrypoint -- Student C
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------
package "AI Phase entrypoint (Student C)" #FBE6D4 {

  class AiPhaseEntrypoint {
    -client : IGradingClient
    -grader : AIGradingComponent
    --
    +main() : int
    --
    A command the instructor's
    run_autograder invokes after her
    test suite exits.
    --
    Resolves marks, errors if a
    registered target was never
    reported, writes a tests-only
    results.json, then grades the marked
    tasks if grading_mode is IMMEDIATE
    or leaves them NEEDED if NIGHTLY,
    and overwrites results.json.
  }

  class ResultsPackager {
    +to_platform_json(pkg, pending) : dict
    --
    The only code that knows the
    platform's results.json schema.
    --
    Called TWICE per grading run: once
    with test results only before
    grading starts, once with the full
    content after. Last write wins, so a
    container killed mid-grading leaves
    the student with test results rather
    than a bare autograder error.
    --
    `pending` is the tasks still NEEDED.
    A courtesy marker for each is worth
    emitting in NIGHTLY mode.
  }

  note as N_PKG #FFF8DC
    In NIGHTLY mode the first results.json has no
    AI feedback at all, which reads correctly as
    "not graded yet". A one-line marker per
    pending task saying feedback arrives by the
    next morning is a courtesy rather than a
    correctness requirement, but it saves the
    student wondering.
  end note

  AiPhaseEntrypoint --> ResultsPackager
}

' ---------------------------------------------------------------------
' Platform automation -- Student C
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------
package "Platform Integration (Student C)" #FBE6D4 {

  interface ILearningPlatform <<abstract>> {
    +authenticate() : None
    +find_submission(platform_assignment_id,\n platform_submission_id) : SubmissionLocator
    +trigger_rerun(locator) : RerunResult
  }

  class GradescopePlatform {
    -page : playwright.Page
    -selectors : SelectorMap
  }

  class FakePlatform {
    Records rerun calls. Lets the
    trigger be tested with no browser
    and no account.
  }

  class SelectorMap {
    +login_email : str
    +login_password : str
    +assignment_rows : str
    +manage_submissions_link : str
    +submission_rows : str
    +submission_id_attr : str
    +rerun_autograder_button : str
    +rerun_confirm_button : str
    --
    Every CSS selector in one file.
    When Gradescope reskins, this is
    the only thing that changes.
  }

  class NightlyTrigger {
    -platform : ILearningPlatform
    -client : IGradingClient
    --
    +run() : TriggerRunSummary
    --
    Asks the service which submissions
    still have tasks marked ai_needed,
    then clicks rerun on each. Never
    calls an LLM.
  }

  ILearningPlatform <|.. GradescopePlatform
  ILearningPlatform <|.. FakePlatform
  GradescopePlatform --> SelectorMap
  NightlyTrigger ..> ILearningPlatform
}

' ---------------------------------------------------------------------
' AI grading -- Student A. Runs INSIDE the autograder container.
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------
package "AI Grading (Student A)" #D6E4F0 {

  class AIGradingComponent {
    -providers : ILLMProvider[]
    -builder : PromptBuilder
    -comparator : ResponseComparator
    -estimator : ConfidenceEstimator
    -client : IGradingClient
    --
    +grade(task_id) : FeedbackItem
    --
    Same code in both modes. Only the
    caller's timing differs.
  }

  interface ILLMProvider <<abstract>> {
    +name : str
    +model : str
    +generate_feedback(req : FeedbackRequest) : FeedbackResponse
    +estimated_cost(req) : float
  }

  class ClaudeProvider
  class OpenAIProvider
  class GeminiProvider
  class FakeProvider {
    Deterministic canned responses, so
    the test suite runs in CI with no
    API key and no bill.
  }

  class PromptBuilder {
    +build(rubric, guidance,\n outcomes, files) : str
    +version : str
  }

  class ResponseComparator {
    +compare(responses) : Comparison
    +select(responses) : FeedbackResponse
  }

  class ConfidenceEstimator {
    +estimate(responses) : float
  }

  ILLMProvider <|.. ClaudeProvider
  ILLMProvider <|.. OpenAIProvider
  ILLMProvider <|.. GeminiProvider
  ILLMProvider <|.. FakeProvider

  AIGradingComponent o--> "1..*" ILLMProvider
  AIGradingComponent --> PromptBuilder
  AIGradingComponent --> ResponseComparator
  AIGradingComponent --> ConfidenceEstimator
}

AiPhaseEntrypoint --> AIGradingComponent

' ---------------------------------------------------------------------
' Service boundary -- Student B
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------
package "Service Boundary (Student B)" #DCEFD9 {

  interface IGradingClient <<abstract>> {
    +resolve_marks(platform_submission_id) : ResolveResult
    +get_feedback_request(task_id) : FeedbackRequest
    +post_feedback(task_id, result) : None
    +mark_ai_complete(submission_id) : bool
    +get_selected_feedback(submission_id) : FeedbackPackage
    +list_submissions_pending_ai(mode) : SubmissionLocator[]
  }

  class HttpGradingClient {
    -base_url : str
    -assignment_token : str
    --
    Per-assignment bearer token,
    scoped to one assignment's rows.
    Never a DB credential.
  }

  class FakeGradingClient {
    In-memory. Lets the AI phase be
    tested offline.
  }

  interface IGradingRepository <<abstract>> {
    +get_assignment_config(...) : AssignmentConfig
    +upsert_submission(ref) : str
    +record_outcome(...) : None
    +record_ai_request(submission_id, target) : None
    +resolve_marks_and_create_tasks(submission_id) : ResolveResult
    +build_feedback_request(task_id) : FeedbackRequest
    +save_feedback(task_id, result) : None
    +mark_ai_complete_if_all_done(submission_id) : bool
    +get_selected_feedback(...) : FeedbackPackage
    +list_submissions_pending_ai(mode) : SubmissionLocator[]
  }

  class SqlGradingRepository
  class InMemoryRepository

  IGradingClient <|.. HttpGradingClient
  IGradingClient <|.. FakeGradingClient
  IGradingRepository <|.. SqlGradingRepository
  IGradingRepository <|.. InMemoryRepository
}

IReportingClient ..> IGradingClient : over HTTPS
AIGradingComponent ..> IGradingClient
AiPhaseEntrypoint ..> IGradingClient
NightlyTrigger ..> IGradingClient

note as N1 #FFF8DC
  **Why IGradingClient and IGradingRepository
  are separate interfaces.**
  The repository is in-process SQL on our cloud
  host. The client is HTTPS from someone else's
  container. Collapsing them would mean shipping
  database credentials inside the autograder
  zip.

  Note the asymmetry decided in AD-5: the
  container DOES hold the instructor's LLM API
  key, and does NOT hold a database credential.
  It reaches our data only through this client,
  with a per-assignment token scoped to one
  assignment's rows.

  The Web API implements the client surface on
  top of the repository. Keeping them distinct
  is what makes that boundary visible in code
  rather than a deployment convention nobody
  remembers.
end note

note as N2 #FFF8DC
  **resolve_marks_and_create_tasks is where cost
  control lives.** It applies each target's
  feedback_mode and, under AUTOGRADER, the
  requests the instructor's suite made during
  this run. It can only run after her suite has
  exited, because only then is the full request
  set known.

  It also returns the registered targets that
  received no outcome. That is an error, not a
  warning: the AI phase exits non-zero and the
  autograder run fails.

  Pure function of policy plus requests, so it
  is the cheapest thing in the system to
  unit-test and the most expensive to get wrong.
  Student D should cover it first.
end note

note as N3 #FFF8DC
  **mark_ai_complete is conditional on purpose.**
  It sets ai_graded_submitted_at only when no
  task is still NEEDED, and returns whether it
  did. Setting it unconditionally would strand
  failed targets permanently ungraded, because
  the guard short-circuits before the task query
  ever runs.
end note

note as N4 #FFF8DC
  **Every interface ships with a fake.**
  FakeReporter, FakePlatform, FakeProvider,
  FakeGradingClient and InMemoryRepository are
  not extras. They are what lets four people
  work in parallel in week two rather than week
  six, and what makes TR-2 and TR-8 achievable
  with no Gradescope account and no API bill.

  Adding an abstract method means adding it to
  the fake in the same commit.
end note

@enduml
